module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.instrumentation_counters_inside_a_semantic_value_defeat_identity

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data instrumentation_counters_inside_a_semantic_value_defeat_identity: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "instrumentation_counters_inside_a_semantic_value_defeat_identity" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value that carries semantic content also carries counters that observe its own use, which change on every operation. Two values holding the same semantic content compare unequal whenever an operation intervened between them, so an identity keyed on the value (a content-keyed memo, a demand key, a dedup) recurs only inside the windows where no counted operation happened. Every demand across those windows is a guaranteed miss that still pays key construction, stores an entry and keeps the argument alive.",
    "INSTANCE (dissolved, see the last receipt): v2.compiler.parse ParseTableRealization carried memo_hits, memo_misses and memo_lookup_calls beside its entries, furthest failure and carried grammar analysis. parse_table_record_lookup_call, parse_table_record_hit and parse_table_record_miss rebuilt the record on every lookup, so a call taking the table presented the seed eval-frame memo (extdeps.realization.eval_memo) with a key that recurs only until the next lookup (parse_table_with_furthest IS served hits inside such windows, measured on the llv probe), and misses across them. The seed memo still keys each such call, stores one entry and retains every table version (eval_call_memo_put). The repairs that closed the 02_parse quadratic -- the verification equality descending to shared allocations, and the per-insert map key beside #12066's per-push list key -- make each of those demands CHEAP; they do not remove them. That is DESIGN section 2's warning that caching makes redundant work cheap and suppresses the signal that would rank it for deletion.",
    "HARM: bounded per call after the repairs, but unbounded in aggregate: one retained table version per missed table-taking call for the provider scope, and a miss population produced by the carrier rather than by the work. It also put the memo on the parse's hot path, where a verification cost proportional to the table (since repaired) presented under the parser's own name as a grammar defect (the 02_parse list-literal cost that blocked #12377).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. Nothing stops a semantic carrier from embedding its own instrumentation; the repairs only bound the cost.",
    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally impossible for carriers whose identity is consumed. Instrumentation is an observation of an occurrence (std.observation), not a field of the observed value, so a counter belongs in the observation channel beside the value, never inside it. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: the parse's memo statistics (ParseMemoStats) produced by an observation channel the parse threads beside ParseTable, SUFFICIENT FOR ParseTable to compare equal across two calls that did the same semantic work, with every current ParseMemoStats consumer reading the channel instead of the table. The admission side of the same demand population (whether the seed memo should key a call that cannot recur) is the roadmap row eval-memo-admission-rewire-program, not this row.",
    "INSTANCE DISSOLVED BY DELETION, NOT BY THE NAMED CAPABILITY (operator ruling R2 2026-10-08): the parse memo carrier was deleted from v2.compiler.parse -- ParseTableRealization's entries and its memo_hits, memo_misses and memo_lookup_calls fields, ParseMemoStats, parse_table_record_lookup_call, parse_table_record_hit, parse_table_record_miss and parse_table_memo_stats -- because the memo served captures whose occurrence ids were minted on abandoned backtrack paths (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.parse_memo_hit_serves_occurrences_minted_on_an_abandoned_path). The specimen therefore has no live carrier and no counters to move into an observation channel. The class itself is unchanged: nothing yet stops another semantic carrier from embedding its own instrumentation, so the row's rung stays mitigatable and the observation-channel capability remains the trigger for the next instance.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.realization.eval_memo", decl_name: "eval_memo_facts"),
  ],
}
